# Hemp planks trapdoor.
#
# Deliberately mirror-symmetric on both axes: the trapdoor texture is drawn on
# both faces of the block and flips with them, so anything with a reading
# direction -- a glyph, a number, a signature -- comes out backwards half the
# time. The previous version spelled 420 and did exactly that.
#
# Same depth rule as the door: dark lip above each opening, light lip below,
# dark left, light right. The 4px-wide centre mullion grades bright-to-dark
# across its width so it reads as a rounded bar rather than a flat strip, which
# is what vanilla's trapdoors do.
#
# No motif: the leaf lives on the door, and every vanilla trapdoor is plain.
#
#   python3 .claude/skills/minecraft-texture-painter/scripts/mctex.py render \
#     textures-src/hemp_planks_trapdoor.mctex \
#     -o src/main/resources/assets/hempdustry/textures --preview --preview-dir /tmp/tex

@palette hemp
. = none
k = 3E3A26      outer edge, darkest
o = 4E4830      groove, and the shadowed lip of every recess
d = 5A5236      plank shadow
e = 67603E      plank dark
m = 82794E      plank mid
b = 8A8155
g = 948A5E
h = A1976C
w = A89D73      lit lip of every recess
n = 4E525A      iron, shadow
i = 6B6F7A      iron
I = 8C939C      iron, lit

@texture block/hemp_planks_trapdoor 16x16 type=block palette=hemp
kkkkkkkkkkkkkkkk
ohggmbghhhgghhbo
ohhooogbbbooohho
oeo...wdeo...weo
owo...wbwo...wbo
oho...wmbo...who
obo...wmho...wbo
odewwwddddwwwmeo
owwooowwwwooowho
ogo...wbbo...wbo
oho...wbgo...who
odo...wddo...wdo
